{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791772048,"nonce":"Fw5ivSh19Wd0pmgTLozUuUiiNj8=","message":"Decision: with claude installed and no login file or CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, Linux answers missing but macOS answers unknown. Reason: spec says a login a stat cannot see gives unknown, never missing; on macOS the CLI keeps it in the Keychain. On Linux the file is where the CLI keeps it on this host. Note for review: the Linux binary also links libsecret-1, so a future CLI could keep a Linux login in the system keyring; if so this step should become unknown on Linux too.","files":null}]}